    ADAPTER NOTES
    relay_workspace: Use the configured working folder for relative paths and commands; absolute input and output paths may be outside it. Read PDF, DOCX and XLSX directly. A missing file in the workspace does not establish absence elsewhere: locate the actual path before retrying ENOENT. Patch exact text and check exit codes plus resulting files. A persistent preview needs a detached launcher, logs, an owned PID and a stop command; verify its URL. Use relay_find_files when the required path is unknown.
    relay_find_files: Find local filenames or paths using a literal query. The working folder is not the search boundary: omitted path/roots searches the computer; explicit path/roots narrows it. Continue while a cursor is returned, even after an empty page. At the end inspect scanComplete, searchComplete, coverage and errors before claiming absence. Open promising paths with relay_workspace read.
    relay_browser_signin: Use available sign-in, saved-credential and email-verification routes before declaring a login blocker. A sent-code notice does not verify an account. Name the exact unavailable credential/challenge when progress is blocked.
    relay_control: Read actual catalog IDs and workflow revision before editing. Observe presentation fields supply labels/focus, not live evidence. Inspect deployment and trigger receipts.
    relay_agents: Inspect actual saved runs and revisions when controlling agents. A start receipt confirms admission, not completion. Preserve the same shared execution state.
    relay_skills: Read relevant task procedures and use the current owner-edited version. Apply the user's request over conflicting skill defaults. Update a skill when requested using available actions; ordinary work does not require skill maintenance.
    relay_history: Use the history operations actually present in this schema for relevant prior context or diagnosis.
    relay_browser: Open or reuse a relevant contained-browser page. An empty task-owned tabs list is not sign-out. Use search, filters or pagination beyond the first view; inspect a new tab opened by an action. For stale refs with no input sent, take a fresh snapshot and retry. To recover a specific stopped-task page, read its current ownership candidate. Pass tabId unchanged, ownerKey as expectedOwnerKey, url as expectedUrl and documentId as expectedDocumentId to take_ownership.
